A||||6||STUK'N'80s||Thinkin' of switching to digital gauges||||3||
Z||000000||STUK'N'80s||08-28-2001||04:17 AM||||I have been itching on switching my current analog gauges to digital ones on my 85 GT.  I wanted to get more opinions from fellow fanatics on my sudden itching!! here are some Q's I want U all to address for me:<P>1. Are these gauges reliable...like will they short out on me all the time etc...etc<BR>2. Which ones on the current market are the best bang for the cash?? I was thinking of getting the ones from PISA Corp. since they are realistic in price...does anyone use em' by any chance??....Your thoughts please!<BR>3. Will the brightness factor on 85 gauges be an issue....meaning do I have to change my current cluster to a later model one??<BR>4. Are they more or less accurate, especially in regards to gas, voltmeter, and temp. indicators.<P>Please feel free to overwhelm me with pros and cons....I NEED IT!!<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-28-2001||06:20 AM||||1.  Yes.  Some more than others.  I'd suggest you choose a brand and ask about them.<P>2.  I'd wait a little while if it were me.  Cliff might start selling his digigauges before long.  (No.  I don't have any inside info.  I'm just being optomistic.)  They look like the best deal yet.  Reasonably priced, too.<P>3.  No.  The digigauges are replacements for your analog gauges.<P>4.  For the most part, they should be more accurate depending on the display.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
