Z||000006||William Federle||08-28-2001||09:29 PM||||I have a 1984 SE and I replaced my Speedometer with a Nordskog 3.5" digital guage. It is readable in direct sunlight, but it looks better if the sunlight isn't direct. Every once in a while the gage flickers and has to be reset by shutting it off and on. I think it may be a problem with the connection to the engine block. Now I have a wire to a connector which then goes to the block - to make it easy to disconnect the gage cluster. It may not be a reliable ground.<P>I then put in a Nordskog 3.5" digital tach.<BR>I was disappointed to find that the tach only reads the hundreds of RPM. I thought it would read at least to the 10's of RPM's.<P>When I replaced the tach, I lost the voltmeter that was on the original tach, so I purchased a digital panel meter from radio shack for 29.00. I had to use a 3 pin regulator to get 5 volts to run the voltmeter. I had to cut a rectangular hole in the black instrument cluster cover above the tach. It didn't turn out bad.<P>Nordskog also makes a full digital panel for various years of camaros - but I don't know if the speedometer would be compatible with the speed sensor on the Fiero. Also, they cost $389.00 If the speedometer was compatible and if you can get past the cost, that would be the best digital panel except for Cliff's which is made for the Fiero.<P>Sorry I'm so long-winded.||||reg||1
